{
  "id": "h1",
  "order": 1,
  "title": "Your fingers have numbers",
  "summary": "Thumb is 1, little finger is 5, on both hands.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Finger numbers",
      "body": "Pianists give each finger a number, so a teacher or a page of music can say which finger to use.\n\n**Finger numbers**: your thumb is 1, the pointing finger is 2, the middle finger is 3, the ring finger is 4 and the little finger is 5. Both hands count the same way, always starting from the thumb.\n\n**Why it matters:** music often prints a small number over a note to tell you which finger plays it, and every hand exercise in this app uses these numbers.\n\nPress **Watch** to see the right hand count 1 to 5.",
      "hands": [
        {
          "hand": "right",
          "keys": [
            60,
            62,
            64,
            65,
            67
          ]
        }
      ],
      "demo": [
