    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "How this app checks you",
      "body": "Your keyboard tells the app which key went down, but not which finger pressed it.\n\nSo the hand on screen shows the finger to use, the key to play glows, and the app marks the key right or wrong. Look at your own hand now and then, and copy the hand on screen.\n\nAfter each run you also get a **steadiness** score: how even the gaps between your notes were, like the ticks of a clock. Slow and even beats fast and bumpy.",
      "hands": [
        {
          "hand": "left",
          "keys": [
            55,
            53,
            52,
            50,
            48
          ]
        },
        {
          "hand": "right",
          "keys": [
